    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d256-a6">

                <pb facs="0451" n="417" xml:id="pg417"/>

                <head>Lord Granville to Sir
                        John Young.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colonial Office,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1870-04-30"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 30, 1870.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to transmit to you the
                    copy of a letter which I have caused to be addressed to the admiralty respecting
                    the instructions to be given to the officers of her. Majesty’s ships employed in
                    the protection of the Canadian fisheries.</p>
                <p>Her Majesty’s government do not doubt that your ministers will agree with them as
                    to the propriety of these instructions, and will give corresponding instructions
                    to the vessels employed by them.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GRANVILLE.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His excellency the Right Honorable Sir <hi rendition="#small-caps">John
                            Young,</hi> Baronet, <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.,
                            &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
